specified by [[dataFile]] or overriding [[getData()]] if you want to use code to generate the fixture data.

When the fixture is being loaded, it will first call [[resetTable()]] to remove any existing data in the table.
It will then populate the table with the data returned by [[getData()]].

After the fixture is loaded, you can access the loaded data via the [[data]] property. If you set [[modelClass]],
you will also be able to retrieve an instance of [[modelClass]] with the populated data via [[getModel()]].

For more details and usage information on ActiveFixture, see the [guide article on fixtures](guide:test-fixtures).";s:5:"since";s:3:"2.0";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:51:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\PropertyRead":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:11:"tableSchema";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Object_":1:{s:45:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Object_␀fqsen";O:30:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen":2:{s:37:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen␀fqsen";s:19:"\yii\db\TableSchema";s:36:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen␀name";s:11:"TableSchema";}}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:13:"property-read";s:14:"␀*␀description";r:938;}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:18:"yii\test\DbFixture";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ClassDoc":26:{s:11:"parentClass";s:16:"yii\test\Fixture";s:10:"isAbstract";b:1;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:10:"interfaces";a:0:{}s:6:"traits";a:0:{}s:10:"subclasses";a:0:{}s:6:"events";a:0:{}s:9:"constants";a:0:{}s:7:"authors";a:1:{s:9:"Qiang Xue";s:19:"qiang.xue@gmail.com";}s:7:"methods";a:1:{s:4:"init";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:18:"yii\test\DbFixture";s:10:"sourceCode";s:117:"public function init()
