If not set, [[\yii\base\Application::language]] will be used.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:9:"$language";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:11:"string|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:6:"string";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:18:"yii\i18n\Formatter";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:2299;s:4:"name";s:9:"$language";s:8:"fullName";s:29:"yii\i18n\Formatter::$language";s:10:"sourceFile";s:93:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/i18n/Formatter.php";s:9:"startLine";i:107;s:7:"endLine";i:107;s:16:"shortDescription";s:83:"The language code (e.g. `en-US`, `en`) that is used to translate internal messages.";s:11:"description";s:165:"The language code (e.g. `en-US`, `en`) that is used to translate internal messages.
If not set, [[locale]] will be used (without the `@calendar` param, if included).";s:5:"since";s:6:"2.0.28";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:36:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Null_":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:165:"the language code (e.g. `en-US`, `en`) that is used to translate internal messages.
If not set, [[locale]] will be used (without the `@calendar` param, if included).";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:9:"$timeZone";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:11:"string|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:6:"string";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:18:"yii\i18n\Formatter";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:2299;s:4:"name";s:9:"$timeZone";s:8:"fullName";s:29:"yii\i18n\Formatter::$timeZone";s:10:"sourceFile";s:93:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/i18n/Formatter.php";s:9:"startLine";i:119;s:7:"endLine";i:119;s:16:"shortDescription";s:57:"The time zone to use for formatting time and date values.";s:11:"description";s:678:"The time zone to use for formatting time and date values.

This can be any value that may be passed to [date_default_timezone_set()](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.date-default-timezone-set.php)
e.g. `UTC`, `Europe/Berlin` or `America/Chicago`.
Refer to the [php manual](https://www.php.net/manual/en/timezones.php) for available time zones.
If this property is not set, [[\yii\base\Application::timeZone]] will be used.

Note that the default time zone for input data is assumed to be UTC by default if no time zone is included in the input date value.
If you store your data in a different time zone in the database, you have to adjust [[defaultTimeZone]] accordingly.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:36:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Null_":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:678:"the time zone to use for formatting time and date values.

This can be any value that may be passed to [date_default_timezone_set()](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.date-default-timezone-set.php)
e.g. `UTC`, `Europe/Berlin` or `America/Chicago`.
Refer to the [php manual](https://www.php.net/manual/en/timezones.php) for available time zones.
If this property is not set, [[\yii\base\Application::timeZone]] will be used.

Note that the default time zone for input data is assumed to be UTC by default if no time zone is included in the input date value.
If you store your data in a different time zone in the database, you have to adjust [[defaultTimeZone]] accordingly.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:16:"$defaultTimeZone";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:5:"'UTC'";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:18:"yii\i18n\Formatter";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:2299;s:4:"name";s:16:"$defaultTimeZone";s:8:"fullName";s:36:"yii\i18n\Formatter::$defaultTimeZone";s:10:"sourceFile";s:93:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/i18n/Formatter.php";s:9:"startLine";i:133;s:7:"endLine";i:133;s:16:"shortDescription";s:93:"The time zone that is assumed for input values if they do not include a time zone explicitly.";s:11:"description";s:608:"The time zone that is assumed for input values if they do not include a time zone explicitly.

The value must be a valid time zone identifier, e.g. `UTC`, `Europe/Berlin` or `America/Chicago`.
Please refer to the [php manual](https://www.php.net/manual/en/timezones.php) for available time zones.

It defaults to `UTC` so you only have to adjust this value if you store datetime values in another time zone in your database.

Note that a UNIX timestamp is always in UTC by its definition. That means that specifying a default time zone different from
UTC has no effect on date values given as UNIX timestamp.";s:5:"since";s:5:"2.0.1";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:608:"the time zone that is assumed for input values if they do not include a time zone explicitly.

The value must be a valid time zone identifier, e.g. `UTC`, `Europe/Berlin` or `America/Chicago`.
Please refer to the [php manual](https://www.php.net/manual/en/timezones.php) for available time zones.

It defaults to `UTC` so you only have to adjust this value if you store datetime values in another time zone in your database.

Note that a UNIX timestamp is always in UTC by its definition. That means that specifying a default time zone different from
UTC has no effect on date values given as UNIX timestamp.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:11:"$dateFormat";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:8:"'medium'";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:18:"yii\i18n\Formatter";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:2299;s:4:"name";s:11:"$dateFormat";s:8:"fullName";s:31:"yii\i18n\Formatter::$dateFormat";s:10:"sourceFile";s:93:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/i18n/Formatter.php";s:9:"startLine";i:149;s:7:"endLine";i:149;s:16:"shortDescription";s:67:"The default format string to be used to format a [[asDate()|date]].";s:11:"description";s:587:"The default format string to be used to format a [[asDate()|date]].
This can be "short", "medium", "long", or "full", which represents a preset format of different lengths.

It can also be a custom format as specified in the [ICU manual](https://unicode-org.github.io/icu/userguide/format_parse/datetime/).
Alternatively this can be a string prefixed with `php:` representing a format that can be recognized by the
PHP [date()](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.date.php)-function.

For example:

```
'MM/dd/yyyy' // date in ICU format
'php:m/d/Y' // the same date in PHP format
```";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:587:"the default format string to be used to format a [[asDate()|date]].
