If [[useFileTransport]] is true, it will save the email as a file under [[fileTransportPath]].
Otherwise, it will call [[sendMessage()]] to send the email to its recipient(s).
Child classes should implement [[sendMessage()]] with the actual email sending logic.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:12:"sendMultiple";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\mail\BaseMailer";s:10:"sourceCode";s:219:"public function sendMultiple(array $messages)
{
    $successCount = 0;
    foreach ($messages as $message) {
        if ($this->send($message)) {
            $successCount++;
        }
    }
    return $successCount;
}
