Additional definitions can be set through the [[definitions]] property.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:12:"$definitions";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:10:"array|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:5:"array";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:23:"yii\widgets\MaskedInput";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:17971;s:4:"name";s:12:"$definitions";s:8:"fullName";s:37:"yii\widgets\MaskedInput::$definitions";s:10:"sourceFile";s:98:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/widgets/MaskedInput.php";s:9:"startLine";i:76;s:7:"endLine";i:76;s:16:"shortDescription";s:31:"Custom mask definitions to use.";s:11:"description";s:616:"Custom mask definitions to use. Should be configured as `maskSymbol => settings`, where

- `maskSymbol` is a string, containing a character to identify your mask definition and
- `settings` is an array, consisting of the following entries:
  - `validator`: string, a JS regular expression or a JS function.
  - `cardinality`: int, specifies how many characters are represented and validated for the definition.
  - `prevalidator`: array, validate the characters before the definition cardinality is reached.
  - `definitionSymbol`: string, allows shifting values from other definitions, with this `definitionSymbol`.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Array_":3:{s:12:"␀*␀valueType";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Mixed_":0:{}s:10:"␀*␀keyType";N;s:17:"␀*␀defaultKeyType";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Integer":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}}i:1;O:36:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Null_":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:616:"custom mask definitions to use. Should be configured as `maskSymbol => settings`, where

- `maskSymbol` is a string, containing a character to identify your mask definition and
- `settings` is an array, consisting of the following entries:
  - `validator`: string, a JS regular expression or a JS function.
  - `cardinality`: int, specifies how many characters are represented and validated for the definition.
  - `prevalidator`: array, validate the characters before the definition cardinality is reached.
