e";s:11:"yii\widgets";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:24942;s:4:"name";s:28:"yii\widgets\ContentDecorator";s:8:"fullName";s:28:"yii\widgets\ContentDecorator";s:10:"sourceFile";s:103:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/widgets/ContentDecorator.php";s:9:"startLine";i:43;s:7:"endLine";i:81;s:16:"shortDescription";s:157:"ContentDecorator records all output between [[begin()]] and [[end()]] calls, passes it to the given view file
as `$content` and then echoes rendering result.";s:11:"description";s:515:"```
<?php ContentDecorator::begin([
    'viewFile' => '@app/views/layouts/base.php',
    'params' => [],
    'view' => $this,
]) ?>

some content here

<?php ContentDecorator::end() ?>
```

There are [[\yii\base\View::beginContent()]] and [[\yii\base\View::endContent()]] wrapper methods in the
[[\yii\base\View]] component to make syntax more friendly. In the view these could be used as follows:

```
<?php $this->beginContent('@app/views/layouts/base.php') ?>

some content here

<?php $this->endContent() ?>
