}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}}s:10:"properties";a:1:{s:8:"$actions";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:5:"array";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:5:"array";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:2:"[]";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:22:"yii\filters\VerbFilter";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:50331;s:4:"name";s:8:"$actions";s:8:"fullName";s:32:"yii\filters\VerbFilter::$actions";s:10:"sourceFile";s:97:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/filters/VerbFilter.php";s:9:"startLine";i:78;s:7:"endLine";i:78;s:16:"shortDescription";s:66:"This property defines the allowed request methods for each action.";s:11:"description";s:470:"This property defines the allowed request methods for each action.
For each action that should only support limited set of request methods
you add an entry with the action id as array key and an array of
allowed methods (e.g. GET, HEAD, PUT) as the value.
If an action is not listed all request methods are considered allowed.

You can use `'*'` to stand for all actions. When an action is explicitly
specified, it takes precedence over the specification given by `'*'`.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:2:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Array_":3:{s:12:"␀*␀valueType";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Mixed_":0:{}s:10:"␀*␀keyType";N;s:17:"␀*␀defaultKeyType";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Integer":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:470:"this property defines the allowed request methods for each action.
For each action that should only support limited set of request methods
you add an entry with the action id as array key and an array of
allowed methods (e.g. GET, HEAD, PUT) as the value.
If an action is not listed all request methods are considered allowed.

You can use `'*'` to stand for all actions. When an action is explicitly
specified, it takes precedence over the specification given by `'*'`.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}i:1;O:42:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\See":3:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"see";s:9:"␀*␀refers";O:52:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Reference\Url":1:{s:57:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Reference\Url␀uri";s:78:"https://www.yiiframework.com/doc/guide/2.0/en/structure-controllers#action-ids";}s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:188:"For example,

```
[
  'create' => ['GET', 'POST'],
  'update' => ['GET', 'PUT', 'POST'],
  'delete' => ['POST', 'DELETE'],
  'author-comment' => ['POST', 'DELETE'],
  '*' => ['GET'],
]
```";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}}s:9:"namespace";s:11:"yii\filters";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:50331;s:4:"name";s:22:"yii\filters\VerbFilter";s:8:"fullName";s:22:"yii\filters\VerbFilter";s:10:"sourceFile";s:97:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/filters/VerbFilter.php";s:9:"startLine";i:52;s:7:"endLine";i:120;s:16:"shortDescription";s:68:"VerbFilter is an action filter that filters by HTTP request methods.";s:11:"description";s:739:"It allows to define allowed HTTP request methods for each action and will throw
an HTTP 405 error when the method is not allowed.

To use VerbFilter, declare it in the `behaviors()` method of your controller class.
For example, the following declarations will define a typical set of allowed
request methods for REST CRUD actions.

```
public function behaviors()
{
    return [
        'verbs' => [
            'class' => \yii\filters\VerbFilter::class,
            'actions' => [
                'index'  => ['GET'],
                'view'   => ['GET'],
                'create' => ['GET', 'POST'],
                'update' => ['GET', 'PUT', 'POST'],
                'delete' => ['POST', 'DELETE'],
            ],
        ],
    ];
}
