Since most browsers only support "post" and "get", if other methods are given, they will
be simulated using "post", and a hidden input will be added which contains the actual method type.
See [[\yii\web\Request::methodParam]] for more details.";s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:95:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseHtml.php";}s:8:"$options";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:8:"$options";s:10:"isOptional";b:1;s:12:"defaultValue";s:2:"[]";s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:401:"The tag options in terms of name-value pairs. These will be rendered as
