about attribute expression.";s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:95:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseHtml.php";}s:8:"$options";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:8:"$options";s:10:"isOptional";b:1;s:12:"defaultValue";s:2:"[]";s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:837:"The tag options in terms of name-value pairs. These will be rendered as
the attributes of the resulting tag. The values will be HTML-encoded using [[encode()]].
See [[renderTagAttributes()]] for details on how attributes are being rendered.
The following special options are recognized:

- maxlength: integer|boolean, when `maxlength` is set true and the model attribute is validated
  by a string validator, the `maxlength` option will take the max value of [[\yii\validators\StringValidator::max]]
  and [[\yii\validators\StringValidator::length].
  This is available since version 2.0.3 and improved taking `length` into account since version 2.0.42.
