for the specified attribute. The name is generated according to the [[Model::formName|form name]]
of the model and the given attribute name. For example, if the form name of the `Post` model
is `Post`, then the input name generated for the `content` attribute would be `Post[content]`.

See [[getAttributeName()]] for explanation of attribute expression.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:16:"getInputIdByName";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:20:"yii\helpers\BaseHtml";s:10:"sourceCode";s:258:"public static function getInputIdByName($name)
{
    $charset = Yii::$app ? Yii::$app->charset : 'UTF-8';
    $name = mb_strtolower($name, $charset);
    return str_replace(['[]', '][', '[', ']', ' ', '.', '--'], ['', '-', '-', '', '-', '-', '-'], $name);
}
