using the `$options` parameter. See the documentation of the [[tag()]] method for more details.

For more details and usage information on Html, see the [guide article on html helpers](guide:helper-html).";s:5:"since";s:3:"2.0";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:19:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ClassDoc":26:{s:11:"parentClass";N;s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:10:"interfaces";a:0:{}s:6:"traits";a:0:{}s:10:"subclasses";a:0:{}s:6:"events";a:0:{}s:9:"constants";a:0:{}s:7:"authors";a:1:{s:17:"Alexander Makarov";s:17:"sam@rmcreative.ru";}s:7:"methods";a:12:{s:7:"toRoute";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl";s:10:"sourceCode";s:334:"public static function toRoute($route, $scheme = false)
{
    $route = (array) $route;
    $route[0] = static::normalizeRoute($route[0]);
    if ($scheme !== false) {
        return static::getUrlManager()->createAbsoluteUrl($route, is_string($scheme) ? $scheme : null);
    }
    return static::getUrlManager()->createUrl($route);
}
";s:6:"params";a:2:{s:6:"$route";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:6:"$route";s:10:"isOptional";b:0;s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:165:"Use a string to represent a route (e.g. `index`, `site/index`),
or an array to represent a route with query parameters (e.g. `['site/index', 'param1' => 'value1']`).";s:4:"type";s:12:"string|array";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:6:"string";i:1;s:5:"array";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}s:7:"$scheme";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:7:"$scheme";s:10:"isOptional";b:1;s:12:"defaultValue";s:5:"false";s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:338:"The URI scheme to use in the generated URL:

- `false` (default): generating a relative URL.
- `true`: returning an absolute base URL whose scheme is the same as that in [[\yii\web\UrlManager::$hostInfo]].
- string: generating an absolute URL with the specified scheme (either `http`, `https` or empty string
  for protocol-relative URL).";s:4:"type";s:11:"bool|string";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:4:"bool";i:1;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:1:{s:34:"\yii\base\InvalidArgumentException";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:61:"a relative route is given while there is no active controller";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}s:6:"return";s:17:"The generated URL";s:10:"returnType";s:6:"string";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Context":2:{s:49:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Context␀namespace";s:11:"yii\helpers";s:56:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Context␀namespaceAliases";a:2:{s:3:"Yii";s:3:"Yii";s:24:"InvalidArgumentException";s:33:"yii\base\InvalidArgumentException";}}s:4:"name";s:7:"toRoute";s:8:"fullName";s:28:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl::toRoute";s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";s:9:"startLine";i:96;s:7:"endLine";i:106;s:16:"shortDescription";s:34:"Creates a URL for the given route.";s:11:"description";s:2071:"This method will use [[\yii\web\UrlManager]] to create a URL.

You may specify the route as a string, e.g., `site/index`. You may also use an array
if you want to specify additional query parameters for the URL being created. The
array format must be:

```
// generates: /index.php?r=site/index&param1=value1&param2=value2
['site/index', 'param1' => 'value1', 'param2' => 'value2']
```

If you want to create a URL with an anchor, you can use the array format with a `#` parameter.
For example,

```
// generates: /index.php?r=site/index&param1=value1#name
['site/index', 'param1' => 'value1', '#' => 'name']
```

A route may be either absolute or relative. An absolute route has a leading slash (e.g. `/site/index`),
while a relative route has none (e.g. `site/index` or `index`). A relative route will be converted
into an absolute one by the following rules:

- If the route is an empty string, the current [[\yii\web\Controller::route|route]] will be used;
- If the route contains no slashes at all (e.g. `index`), it is considered to be an action ID
  of the current controller and will be prepended with [[\yii\web\Controller::uniqueId]];
- If the route has no leading slash (e.g. `site/index`), it is considered to be a route relative
  to the current module and will be prepended with the module's [[\yii\base\Module::uniqueId|uniqueId]].

Starting from version 2.0.2, a route can also be specified as an alias. In this case, the alias
will be converted into the actual route first before conducting the above transformation steps.

Below are some examples of using this method:

```
// /index.php?r=site%2Findex
echo Url::toRoute('site/index');

// /index.php?r=site%2Findex&src=ref1#name
echo Url::toRoute(['site/index', 'src' => 'ref1', '#' => 'name']);

// https://www.example.com/index.php?r=site%2Findex
echo Url::toRoute('site/index', true);

// https://www.example.com/index.php?r=site%2Findex
echo Url::toRoute('site/index', 'https');

// /index.php?r=post%2Findex     assume the alias "@posts" is defined as "post/index"
echo Url::toRoute('@posts');
```";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:14:"normalizeRoute";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:9:"protected";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl";s:10:"sourceCode";s:714:"protected static function normalizeRoute($route)
{
    $route = Yii::getAlias((string) $route);
    if (strncmp($route, '/', 1) === 0) {
        // absolute route
        return ltrim($route, '/');
    }
    // relative route
    if (Yii::$app->controller === null) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException("Unable to resolve the relative route: $route. No active controller is available.");
    }
    if (strpos($route, '/') === false) {
        // empty or an action ID
        return $route === '' ? Yii::$app->controller->getRoute() : Yii::$app->controller->getUniqueId() . '/' . $route;
    }
    // relative to module
    return ltrim(Yii::$app->controller->module->getUniqueId() . '/' . $route, '/');
}
";s:6:"params";a:1:{s:6:"$route";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:6:"$route";s:10:"isOptional";b:0;s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:68:"The route. This can be either an absolute route or a relative route.";s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:1:{s:34:"\yii\base\InvalidArgumentException";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:61:"a relative route is given while there is no active controller";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}s:6:"return";s:40:"Normalized route suitable for UrlManager";s:10:"returnType";s:6:"string";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:64477;s:4:"name";s:14:"normalizeRoute";s:8:"fullName";s:35:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl::normalizeRoute";s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";s:9:"startLine";i:127;s:7:"endLine";i:147;s:16:"shortDescription";s:142:"Normalizes route and makes it suitable for UrlManager. Absolute routes are staying as is
while relative routes are converted to absolute ones.";s:11:"description";s:693:"A relative route is a route without a leading slash, such as "view", "post/view".

- If the route is an empty string, the current [[\yii\web\Controller::route|route]] will be used;
- If the route contains no slashes at all, it is considered to be an action ID
  of the current controller and will be prepended with [[\yii\web\Controller::uniqueId]];
- If the route has no leading slash, it is considered to be a route relative
  to the current module and will be prepended with the module's uniqueId.

Starting from version 2.0.2, a route can also be specified as an alias. In this case, the alias
will be converted into the actual route first before conducting the above transformation steps.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:2:"to";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl";s:10:"sourceCode";s:517:"public static function to($url = '', $scheme = false)
{
    if (is_array($url)) {
        return static::toRoute($url, $scheme);
    }
    $url = Yii::getAlias($url);
    if ($url === '') {
        $url = Yii::$app->getRequest()->getUrl();
    }
    if ($scheme === false) {
        return $url;
    }
    if (static::isRelative($url)) {
        // turn relative URL into absolute
        $url = static::getUrlManager()->getHostInfo() . '/' . ltrim($url, '/');
    }
    return static::ensureScheme($url, $scheme);
}
";s:6:"params";a:2:{s:4:"$url";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:4:"$url";s:10:"isOptional";b:1;s:12:"defaultValue";s:2:"''";s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:48:"The parameter to be used to generate a valid URL";s:4:"type";s:12:"array|string";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:5:"array";i:1;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}s:7:"$scheme";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:7:"$scheme";s:10:"isOptional";b:1;s:12:"defaultValue";s:5:"false";s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:338:"The URI scheme to use in the generated URL:

- `false` (default): generating a relative URL.
- `true`: returning an absolute base URL whose scheme is the same as that in [[\yii\web\UrlManager::$hostInfo]].
- string: generating an absolute URL with the specified scheme (either `http`, `https` or empty string
  for protocol-relative URL).";s:4:"type";s:11:"bool|string";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:4:"bool";i:1;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:1:{s:34:"\yii\base\InvalidArgumentException";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:61:"a relative route is given while there is no active controller";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}s:6:"return";s:17:"The generated URL";s:10:"returnType";s:6:"string";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:64477;s:4:"name";s:2:"to";s:8:"fullName";s:23:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl::to";s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";s:9:"startLine";i:211;s:7:"endLine";i:232;s:16:"shortDescription";s:44:"Creates a URL based on the given parameters.";s:11:"description";s:1646:"This method is very similar to [[toRoute()]]. The only difference is that this method
requires a route to be specified as an array only. If a string is given, it will be treated as a URL.
In particular, if `$url` is

- an array: [[toRoute()]] will be called to generate the URL. For example:
  `['site/index']`, `['post/index', 'page' => 2]`. Please refer to [[toRoute()]] for more details
  on how to specify a route.
- a string with a leading `@`: it is treated as an alias, and the corresponding aliased string
  will be returned.
- an empty string: the currently requested URL will be returned;
- a normal string: it will be returned as is.

When `$scheme` is specified (either a string or `true`), an absolute URL with host info (obtained from
[[\yii\web\UrlManager::$hostInfo]]) will be returned. If `$url` is already an absolute URL, its scheme
will be replaced with the specified one.

Below are some examples of using this method:

```
// /index.php?r=site%2Findex
echo Url::to(['site/index']);

// /index.php?r=site%2Findex&src=ref1#name
echo Url::to(['site/index', 'src' => 'ref1', '#' => 'name']);

// /index.php?r=post%2Findex     assume the alias "@posts" is defined as "/post/index"
echo Url::to(['@posts']);

// the currently requested URL
echo Url::to();

// /images/logo.gif
echo Url::to('@web/images/logo.gif');

// images/logo.gif
echo Url::to('images/logo.gif');

// https://www.example.com/images/logo.gif
echo Url::to('@web/images/logo.gif', true);

// https://www.example.com/images/logo.gif
echo Url::to('@web/images/logo.gif', 'https');

// //www.example.com/images/logo.gif
echo Url::to('@web/images/logo.gif', '');
```";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:12:"ensureScheme";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl";s:10:"sourceCode";s:511:"public static function ensureScheme($url, $scheme)
{
    if (static::isRelative($url) || !is_string($scheme)) {
        return $url;
    }
    if (strncmp($url, '//', 2) === 0) {
        // e.g. //example.com/path/to/resource
        return $scheme === '' ? $url : "$scheme:$url";
    }
    if (($pos = strpos($url, '://')) !== false) {
        if ($scheme === '') {
            $url = substr($url, $pos + 1);
        } else {
            $url = $scheme . substr($url, $pos);
        }
    }
    return $url;
}
";s:6:"params";a:2:{s:4:"$url";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:4:"$url";s:10:"isOptional";b:0;s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:18:"The URL to process";s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}s:7:"$scheme";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:7:"$scheme";s:10:"isOptional";b:0;s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:136:"The URI scheme used in the URL (e.g. `http` or `https`). Use an empty string to
create protocol-relative URL (e.g. `//example.com/path`)";s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:0:{}s:6:"return";s:17:"The processed URL";s:10:"returnType";s:6:"string";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:64477;s:4:"name";s:12:"ensureScheme";s:8:"fullName";s:33:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl::ensureScheme";s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/helpers/BaseUrl.php";s:9:"startLine";i:245;s:7:"endLine";i:265;s:16:"shortDescription";s:55:"Normalize the URL by ensuring it uses specified scheme.";s:11:"description";s:79:"If the URL is relative or the scheme is not a string, normalization is skipped.";s:5:"since";s:6:"2.0.11";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:4:"base";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\helpers\BaseUrl";s:10:"sourceCode";s:265:"public static function base($scheme = false)
{
    $url = static::getUrlManager()->getBaseUrl();
    if ($scheme !== false) {
        $url = static::getUrlManager()->getHostInfo() . $url;
        $url = static::ensureScheme($url, $scheme);
    }
    return $url;
}
";s:6:"params";a:1:{s:7:"$scheme";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ParamDoc":8:{s:4:"name";s:7:"$scheme";s:10:"isOptional";b:1;s:12:"defaultValue";s:5:"false";s:19:"isPassedByReference";b:0;s:11:"description";s:361:"The URI scheme to use in the returned base URL:

- `false` (default): returning the base URL without host info.
- `true`: returning an absolute base URL whose scheme is the same as that in [[\yii\web\UrlManager::$hostInfo]].
- string: returning an absolute base URL with the specified scheme (either `http`, `https` or empty string
