    '_SERVER',
]";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:14:"yii\log\Target";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:66390;s:4:"name";s:8:"$logVars";s:8:"fullName";s:24:"yii\log\Target::$logVars";s:10:"sourceFile";s:89:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/log/Target.php";s:9:"startLine";i:78;s:7:"endLine";i:85;s:16:"shortDescription";s:72:"List of the PHP predefined variables that should be logged in a message.";s:11:"description";s:606:"List of the PHP predefined variables that should be logged in a message.
Note that a variable must be accessible via `$GLOBALS`. Otherwise it won't be logged.

Defaults to `['_GET', '_POST', '_FILES', '_COOKIE', '_SESSION', '_SERVER']`.

Since version 2.0.9 additional syntax can be used:
Each element could be specified as one of the following:

- `var` - `var` will be logged.
- `var.key` - only `var[key]` key will be logged.
- `!var.key` - `var[key]` key will be excluded.

Note that if you need $_SESSION to logged regardless if session was used you have to open it right at
the start of your request.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:2:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Array_":3:{s:12:"␀*␀valueType";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Mixed_":0:{}s:10:"␀*␀keyType";N;s:17:"␀*␀defaultKeyType";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Integer":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:606:"list of the PHP predefined variables that should be logged in a message.
Note that a variable must be accessible via `$GLOBALS`. Otherwise it won't be logged.

Defaults to `['_GET', '_POST', '_FILES', '_COOKIE', '_SESSION', '_SERVER']`.

Since version 2.0.9 additional syntax can be used:
Each element could be specified as one of the following:

- `var` - `var` will be logged.
- `var.key` - only `var[key]` key will be logged.
- `!var.key` - `var[key]` key will be excluded.

Note that if you need $_SESSION to logged regardless if session was used you have to open it right at
the start of your request.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}i:1;O:42:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\See":3:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"see";s:9:"␀*␀refers";O:54:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Reference\Fqsen":1:{s:61:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Reference\Fqsen␀fqsen";O:30:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen":2:{s:37:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen␀fqsen";s:34:"\yii\helpers\ArrayHelper::filter()";s:36:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen␀name";s:6:"filter";}}s:14:"␀*␀description";N;}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:9:"$maskVars";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:5:"array";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:5:"array";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:93:"[
    '_SERVER.HTTP_AUTHORIZATION',
    '_SERVER.PHP_AUTH_USER',
    '_SERVER.PHP_AUTH_PW',
]";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:14:"yii\log\Target";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:66390;s:4:"name";s:9:"$maskVars";s:8:"fullName";s:25:"yii\log\Target::$maskVars";s:10:"sourceFile";s:89:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/log/Target.php";s:9:"startLine";i:104;s:7:"endLine";i:108;s:16:"shortDescription";s:146:"List of the PHP predefined variables that should NOT be logged "as is" and should always be replaced with a mask `***` before logging, when exist.";s:11:"description";s:743:"List of the PHP predefined variables that should NOT be logged "as is" and should always be replaced
with a mask `***` before logging, when exist.

Defaults to `[ '_SERVER.HTTP_AUTHORIZATION', '_SERVER.PHP_AUTH_USER', '_SERVER.PHP_AUTH_PW']`

Each element could be specified as one of the following:

- `var` - `var` will be logged as `***`
- `var.key` - only `var[key]` will be logged as `***`

In addition, this property accepts (case-insensitive) patterns. For example:
- `_SERVER.*_SECRET` matches all ending with `_SECRET`, such as `$_SERVER['TOKEN_SECRET']` etc.
- `_SERVER.SECRET_*` matches all starting with `SECRET_`, such as `$_SERVER['SECRET_TOKEN']` etc.
- `_SERVER.*SECRET*` matches all containing `SECRET` i.e. both of the above.";s:5:"since";s:6:"2.0.16";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Array_":3:{s:12:"␀*␀valueType";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Mixed_":0:{}s:10:"␀*␀keyType";N;s:17:"␀*␀defaultKeyType";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Integer":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:743:"list of the PHP predefined variables that should NOT be logged "as is" and should always be replaced
with a mask `***` before logging, when exist.

Defaults to `[ '_SERVER.HTTP_AUTHORIZATION', '_SERVER.PHP_AUTH_USER', '_SERVER.PHP_AUTH_PW']`

Each element could be specified as one of the following:

- `var` - `var` will be logged as `***`
- `var.key` - only `var[key]` will be logged as `***`

In addition, this property accepts (case-insensitive) patterns. For example:
- `_SERVER.*_SECRET` matches all ending with `_SECRET`, such as `$_SERVER['TOKEN_SECRET']` etc.
- `_SERVER.SECRET_*` matches all starting with `SECRET_`, such as `$_SERVER['SECRET_TOKEN']` etc.
- `_SERVER.*SECRET*` matches all containing `SECRET` i.e. both of the above.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:7:"$prefix";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:13:"callable|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:8:"callable";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:14:"yii\log\Target";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:66390;s:4:"name";s:7:"$prefix";s:8:"fullName";s:23:"yii\log\Target::$prefix";s:10:"sourceFile";s:89:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/log/Target.php";s:9:"startLine";i:117;s:7:"endLine";i:117;s:16:"shortDescription";s:78:"A PHP callable that returns a string to be prefixed to every exported message.";s:11:"description";s:285:"A PHP callable that returns a string to be prefixed to every exported message.

