";s:6:"params";a:0:{}s:10:"exceptions";a:0:{}s:6:"return";s:32:"Attribute labels (name => label)";s:10:"returnType";s:5:"array";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:5:"array";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:83412;s:4:"name";s:15:"attributeLabels";s:8:"fullName";s:31:"yii\base\Model::attributeLabels";s:10:"sourceFile";s:89:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/base/Model.php";s:9:"startLine";i:339;s:7:"endLine";i:342;s:16:"shortDescription";s:29:"Returns the attribute labels.";s:11:"description";s:509:"Attribute labels are mainly used for display purpose. For example, given an attribute
`firstName`, we can declare a label `First Name` which is more user-friendly and can
be displayed to end users.

By default an attribute label is generated using [[generateAttributeLabel()]].
This method allows you to explicitly specify attribute labels.

Note, in order to inherit labels defined in the parent class, a child class needs to
