The following criteria are used to determine whether a rule is currently applicable:

- the rule must be associated with the attributes relevant to the current scenario;
- the rules must be effective for the current scenario.

This method will call [[beforeValidate()]] and [[afterValidate()]] before and
after the actual validation, respectively. If [[beforeValidate()]] returns false,
the validation will be cancelled and [[afterValidate()]] will not be called.

Errors found during the validation can be retrieved via [[getErrors()]],
[[getFirstErrors()]] and [[getFirstError()]].";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:14:"beforeValidate";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:14:"yii\base\Model";s:10:"sourceCode";s:153:"public function beforeValidate()
{
    $event = new ModelEvent();
    $this->trigger(self::EVENT_BEFORE_VALIDATE, $event);
    return $event->isValid;
}
