This parameter is available since version 2.0.1.";s:4:"type";s:11:"string|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:6:"string";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:89:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/base/Model.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:0:{}s:6:"return";s:61:"Whether at least one of the models is successfully populated.";s:10:"returnType";s:4:"bool";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:4:"bool";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:83412;s:4:"name";s:12:"loadMultiple";s:8:"fullName";s:28:"yii\base\Model::loadMultiple";s:10:"sourceFile";s:89:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/base/Model.php";s:9:"startLine";i:961;s:7:"endLine";i:985;s:16:"shortDescription";s:54:"Populates a set of models with the data from end user.";s:11:"description";s:412:"This method is mainly used to collect tabular data input.
The data to be loaded for each model is `$data[formName][index]`, where `formName`
refers to the value of [[formName()]], and `index` the index of the model in the `$models` array.
If [[formName()]] is empty, `$data[index]` will be used to populate each model.
The data being populated to each model is subject to the safety check by [[setAttributes()]].";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:16:"validateMultiple";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:1;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:14:"yii\base\Model";s:10:"sourceCode";s:245:"public static function validateMultiple($models, $attributeNames = null)
{
    $valid = true;
    /** @var self $model */
    foreach ($models as $model) {
        $valid = $model->validate($attributeNames) && $valid;
    }
    return $valid;
}
