specified via [[rules]] will take precedence when the same property of the rule is configured.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}}s:9:"namespace";s:7:"yii\web";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:94116;s:4:"name";s:20:"yii\web\GroupUrlRule";s:8:"fullName";s:20:"yii\web\GroupUrlRule";s:10:"sourceFile";s:95:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/web/GroupUrlRule.php";s:9:"startLine";i:48;s:7:"endLine";i:144;s:16:"shortDescription";s:103:"GroupUrlRule represents a collection of URL rules sharing the same prefix in their patterns and routes.";s:11:"description";s:972:"GroupUrlRule is best used by a module which often uses module ID as the prefix for the URL rules.
For example, the following code creates a rule for the `admin` module:

```
new GroupUrlRule([
    'prefix' => 'admin',
    'rules' => [
        'login' => 'user/login',
        'logout' => 'user/logout',
        'dashboard' => 'default/dashboard',
    ],
]);

// the above rule is equivalent to the following three rules:

[
    'admin/login' => 'admin/user/login',
    'admin/logout' => 'admin/user/logout',
    'admin/dashboard' => 'admin/default/dashboard',
]
```

The above example assumes the prefix for patterns and routes are the same. They can be made different
by configuring [[prefix]] and [[routePrefix]] separately.

Using a GroupUrlRule is more efficient than directly declaring the individual rules it contains.
This is because GroupUrlRule can quickly determine if it should process a URL parsing or creation request
by simply checking if the prefix matches.";s:5:"since";s:3:"2.0";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:41:"yii\web\UnsupportedMediaTypeHttpException";O:26:"yii\apidoc\models\ClassDoc":26:{s:11:"parentClass";s:21:"yii\web\HttpException";s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:10:"interfaces";a:0:{}s:6:"traits";a:0:{}s:10:"subclasses";a:0:{}s:6:"events";a:0:{}s:9:"constants";a:0:{}s:7:"authors";a:1:{s:11:"Dan Schmidt";s:24:"danschmidt5189@gmail.com";}s:7:"methods";a:1:{s:11:"__construct";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:41:"yii\web\UnsupportedMediaTypeHttpException";s:10:"sourceCode";s:136:"public function __construct($message = null, $code = 0, $previous = null)
{
    parent::__construct(415, $message, $code, $previous);
}
