last modification time of the published asset file.
You normally would want to set this property to true when you have enabled HTTP caching for assets,
because it allows you to bust caching when the assets are updated.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:13:"$hashCallback";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:13:"callable|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:8:"callable";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:20:"yii\web\AssetManager";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:102062;s:4:"name";s:13:"$hashCallback";s:8:"fullName";s:35:"yii\web\AssetManager::$hashCallback";s:10:"sourceFile";s:95:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/web/AssetManager.php";s:9:"startLine";i:217;s:7:"endLine";i:217;s:16:"shortDescription";s:78:"A callback that will be called to produce hash for asset directory generation.";s:11:"description";s:686:"A callback that will be called to produce hash for asset directory generation.
The signature of the callback should be as follows:

```
function ($path)
```

where `$path` is the asset path. Note that the `$path` can be either directory where the asset
files reside or a single file. For a CSS file that uses relative path in `url()`, the hash
implementation should use the directory path of the file instead of the file path to include
the relative asset files in the copying.

If this is not set, the asset manager will use the default CRC32 and filemtime in the `hash`
method.

Example of an implementation using MD4 hash:

```
function ($path) {
    return hash('md4', $path);
}
```";s:5:"since";s:5:"2.0.6";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:40:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Callable_":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Callable_␀returnType";N;s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Callable_␀parameters";a:0:{}}i:1;O:36:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Null_":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:686:"a callback that will be called to produce hash for asset directory generation.
The signature of the callback should be as follows:

```
function ($path)
```

where `$path` is the asset path. Note that the `$path` can be either directory where the asset
files reside or a single file. For a CSS file that uses relative path in `url()`, the hash
implementation should use the directory path of the file instead of the file path to include
the relative asset files in the copying.

If this is not set, the asset manager will use the default CRC32 and filemtime in the `hash`
method.

Example of an implementation using MD4 hash:

```
function ($path) {
    return hash('md4', $path);
}
```";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}}s:9:"namespace";s:7:"yii\web";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:102062;s:4:"name";s:20:"yii\web\AssetManager";s:8:"fullName";s:20:"yii\web\AssetManager";s:10:"sourceFile";s:95:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/web/AssetManager.php";s:9:"startLine";i:60;s:7:"endLine";i:703;s:16:"shortDescription";s:60:"AssetManager manages asset bundle configuration and loading.";s:11:"description";s:514:"AssetManager is configured as an application component in [[\yii\web\Application]] by default.
You can access that instance via `Yii::$app->assetManager`.

You can modify its configuration by adding an array to your application config under `components`
as shown in the following example:

```
'assetManager' => [
    'bundles' => [
        // you can override AssetBundle configs here
    ],
]
```

For more details and usage information on AssetManager, see the [guide article on assets](guide:structure-assets).";s:5:"since";s:3:"2.0";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:3:{i:0;O:47:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Property":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:9:"converter";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Object_":1:{s:45:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Object_␀fqsen";O:30:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen":2:{s:37:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen␀fqsen";s:32:"\yii\web\AssetConverterInterface";s:36:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Fqsen␀name";s:23:"AssetConverterInterface";}}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:8:"property";s:14:"␀*␀description";r:102824;}i:3;O:46:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Generic":2:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:12:"phpstan-type";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:168:"PublishOptions array{
    only?: string[],
    except?: string[],
    caseSensitive?: bool,
    beforeCopy?: callable,
    afterCopy?: callable,
    forceCopy?: bool,
}";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}i:4;O:46:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Generic":2:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:10:"psalm-type";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:170:"PublishOptions = array{
