Starting from version 2.0.2, this can also be a configuration array for creating the object.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:13:"$sessionTable";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:14:"'{{%session}}'";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:17:"yii\web\DbSession";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:112321;s:4:"name";s:13:"$sessionTable";s:8:"fullName";s:32:"yii\web\DbSession::$sessionTable";s:10:"sourceFile";s:92:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/web/DbSession.php";s:9:"startLine";i:76;s:7:"endLine";i:76;s:16:"shortDescription";s:54:"The name of the DB table that stores the session data.";s:11:"description";s:751:"The name of the DB table that stores the session data.
The table should be pre-created as follows:

```
CREATE TABLE session
(
    id CHAR(40) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    expire INTEGER,
    data BLOB
)
```

where 'BLOB' refers to the BLOB-type of your preferred DBMS. Below are the BLOB type
that can be used for some popular DBMS:

- MySQL: LONGBLOB
- PostgreSQL: BYTEA
- MSSQL: BLOB

When using DbSession in a production server, we recommend you create a DB index for the 'expire'
column in the session table to improve the performance.

Note that according to the php.ini setting of `session.hash_function`, you may need to adjust
the length of the `id` column. For example, if `session.hash_function=sha256`, you should use
length 64 instead of 40.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:751:"the name of the DB table that stores the session data.
The table should be pre-created as follows:

```
CREATE TABLE session
(
    id CHAR(40) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    expire INTEGER,
    data BLOB
)
```

where 'BLOB' refers to the BLOB-type of your preferred DBMS. Below are the BLOB type
that can be used for some popular DBMS:

- MySQL: LONGBLOB
- PostgreSQL: BYTEA
- MSSQL: BLOB

When using DbSession in a production server, we recommend you create a DB index for the 'expire'
column in the session table to improve the performance.

Note that according to the php.ini setting of `session.hash_function`, you may need to adjust
the length of the `id` column. For example, if `session.hash_function=sha256`, you should use
length 64 instead of 40.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:7:"$fields";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:9:"protected";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:5:"array";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:5:"array";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:2:"[]";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:17:"yii\web\DbSession";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:112321;s:4:"name";s:7:"$fields";s:8:"fullName";s:26:"yii\web\DbSession::$fields";s:10:"sourceFile";s:92:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/web/DbSession.php";s:9:"startLine";i:82;s:7:"endLine";i:82;s:16:"shortDescription";s:55:"Session fields to be written into session table columns";s:11:"description";s:55:"Session fields to be written into session table columns";s:5:"since";s:6:"2.0.17";s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Array_":3:{s:12:"␀*␀valueType";O:37:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Mixed_":0:{}s:10:"␀*␀keyType";N;s:17:"␀*␀defaultKeyType";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Integer":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:55:"Session fields to be written into session table columns";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}}s:9:"namespace";s:7:"yii\web";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:112321;s:4:"name";s:17:"yii\web\DbSession";s:8:"fullName";s:17:"yii\web\DbSession";s:10:"sourceFile";s:92:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/web/DbSession.php";s:9:"startLine";i:40;s:7:"endLine";i:288;s:16:"shortDescription";s:72:"DbSession extends [[Session]] by using database as session data storage.";s:11:"description";s:590:"By default, DbSession stores session data in a DB table named 'session'. This table
must be pre-created. The table name can be changed by setting [[sessionTable]].

The following example shows how you can configure the application to use DbSession:
Add the following to your application config under `components`:

```
'session' => [
    'class' => 'yii\web\DbSession',
    // 'db' => 'mydb',
    // 'sessionTable' => 'my_session',
]
```

DbSession extends [[MultiFieldSession]], thus it allows saving extra fields into the [[sessionTable]].
