The table should be pre-created as follows:

```
CREATE TABLE cache (
    id char(128) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    expire int(11),
    data BLOB
);
```

For MSSQL:
```
CREATE TABLE cache (
    id VARCHAR(128) NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    expire INT(11),
    data VARBINARY(MAX)
);
```

where 'BLOB' refers to the BLOB-type of your preferred DBMS. Below are the BLOB type
that can be used for some popular DBMS:

- MySQL: LONGBLOB
- PostgreSQL: BYTEA

When using DbCache in a production server, we recommend you create a DB index for the 'expire'
column in the cache table to improve the performance.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:639:"name of the DB table to store cache content.
