etweenColumnsCondition";s:10:"sourceFile";s:116:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/conditions/BetweenColumnsCondition.php";s:9:"startLine";i:42;s:7:"endLine";i:122;s:16:"shortDescription";s:111:"Class BetweenColumnCondition represents a `BETWEEN` condition where
values is between two columns. For example:";s:11:"description";s:448:"```
new BetweenColumnsCondition(42, 'BETWEEN', 'min_value', 'max_value')
// Will be build to:
// 42 BETWEEN min_value AND max_value
```

And a more complex example:

```
new BetweenColumnsCondition(
   new Expression('NOW()'),
   'NOT BETWEEN',
   (new Query)->select('time')->from('log')->orderBy('id ASC')->limit(1),
   'update_time'
);

// Will be built to:
// NOW() NOT BETWEEN (SELECT time FROM log ORDER BY id ASC LIMIT 1) AND update_time
