1. call [[beforeValidate()]] when `$runValidation` is `true`. If [[beforeValidate()]]
   returns `false`, the rest of the steps will be skipped;
2. call [[afterValidate()]] when `$runValidation` is `true`. If validation
   failed, the rest of the steps will be skipped;
3. call [[beforeSave()]]. If [[beforeSave()]] returns `false`,
   the rest of the steps will be skipped;
4. insert the record into database. If this fails, it will skip the rest of the steps;
5. call [[afterSave()]];

In the above step 1, 2, 3 and 5, events [[EVENT_BEFORE_VALIDATE]],
[[EVENT_AFTER_VALIDATE]], [[EVENT_BEFORE_INSERT]], and [[EVENT_AFTER_INSERT]]
will be raised by the corresponding methods.

Only the [[dirtyAttributes|changed attribute values]] will be inserted into database.

If the table's primary key is auto-incremental and is `null` during insertion,
it will be populated with the actual value after insertion.

For example, to insert a customer record:

```
$customer = new Customer;
$customer->name = $name;
$customer->email = $email;
$customer->insert();
```";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:7:"hasMany";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\db\ActiveRecord";s:10:"sourceCode";s:86:"public function hasMany($class, $link)
