meaning all attributes that are loaded from DB will be saved.";s:4:"type";s:10:"array|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:5:"array";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/ActiveRecord.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:2:{s:28:"\yii\db\StaleObjectException";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:91:"if [[optimisticLock|optimistic locking]] is enabled and the data
being updated is outdated.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}s:10:"\Throwable";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:22:"in case update failed.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}s:6:"return";s:105:"The number of rows affected, or false if validation fails
or [[beforeSave()]] stops the updating process.";s:10:"returnType";s:9:"int|false";s:11:"returnTypes";a:2:{i:0;s:3:"int";i:1;s:5:"false";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:159117;s:4:"name";s:6:"update";s:8:"fullName";s:27:"yii\db\ActiveRecord::update";s:10:"sourceFile";s:94:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/ActiveRecord.php";s:9:"startLine";i:711;s:7:"endLine";i:739;s:16:"shortDescription";s:75:"Saves the changes to this active record into the associated database table.";s:11:"description";s:1285:"This method performs the following steps in order:

1. call [[beforeValidate()]] when `$runValidation` is `true`. If [[beforeValidate()]]
   returns `false`, the rest of the steps will be skipped;
2. call [[afterValidate()]] when `$runValidation` is `true`. If validation
   failed, the rest of the steps will be skipped;
3. call [[beforeSave()]]. If [[beforeSave()]] returns `false`,
   the rest of the steps will be skipped;
4. save the record into database. If this fails, it will skip the rest of the steps;
5. call [[afterSave()]];

In the above step 1, 2, 3 and 5, events [[EVENT_BEFORE_VALIDATE]],
[[EVENT_AFTER_VALIDATE]], [[EVENT_BEFORE_UPDATE]], and [[EVENT_AFTER_UPDATE]]
will be raised by the corresponding methods.

Only the [[dirtyAttributes|changed attribute values]] will be saved into database.

For example, to update a customer record:

```
$customer = Customer::findOne($id);
$customer->name = $name;
$customer->email = $email;
$customer->update();
```

Note that it is possible the update does not affect any row in the table.
In this case, this method will return 0. For this reason, you should use the following
code to check if update() is successful or not:

```
if ($customer->update() !== false) {
    // update successful
} else {
    // update failed
}
```";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:0:{}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:6:"delete";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:19:"yii\db\ActiveRecord";s:10:"sourceCode";s:564:"public function delete()
{
    if (!$this->isTransactional(self::OP_DELETE)) {
        return $this->deleteInternal();
    }
    $transaction = static::getDb()->beginTransaction();
    try {
        $result = $this->deleteInternal();
        if ($result === false) {
            $transaction->rollBack();
        } else {
            $transaction->commit();
        }
        return $result;
    } catch (\Exception $e) {
        $transaction->rollBack();
        throw $e;
    } catch (\Throwable $e) {
        $transaction->rollBack();
        throw $e;
    }
}
