the attributes of the record associated with the `$class` model, while the values of the
array refer to the corresponding attributes in **this** AR class.";s:4:"type";s:5:"array";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:5:"array";}s:10:"sourceFile";s:98:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/BaseActiveRecord.php";}}s:10:"exceptions";a:0:{}s:6:"return";s:28:"The relational query object.";s:10:"returnType";s:28:"\yii\db\ActiveQueryInterface";s:11:"returnTypes";a:1:{i:0;s:28:"\yii\db\ActiveQueryInterface";}s:19:"isReturnByReference";b:0;s:13:"phpDocContext";r:170608;s:4:"name";s:6:"hasOne";s:8:"fullName";s:31:"yii\db\BaseActiveRecord::hasOne";s:10:"sourceFile";s:98:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/BaseActiveRecord.php";s:9:"startLine";i:399;s:7:"endLine";i:402;s:16:"shortDescription";s:30:"Declares a `has-one` relation.";s:11:"description";s:809:"The declaration is returned in terms of a relational [[ActiveQuery]] instance
through which the related record can be queried and retrieved back.

A `has-one` relation means that there is at most one related record matching
the criteria set by this relation, e.g., a customer has one country.

For example, to declare the `country` relation for `Customer` class, we can write
the following code in the `Customer` class:

```
public function getCountry()
{
    return $this->hasOne(Country::class, ['id' => 'country_id']);
}
```

Note that in the above, the 'id' key in the `$link` parameter refers to an attribute name
in the related class `Country`, while the 'country_id' value refers to an attribute name
in the current AR class.

Call methods declared in [[ActiveQuery]] to further customize the relation.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:4:{i:3;O:46:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Generic":2:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:13:"phpstan-param";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:19:"class-string $class";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}i:4;O:46:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Generic":2:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:11:"psalm-param";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:19:"class-string $class";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}i:5;O:46:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Generic":2:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:13:"phpstan-param";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:27:"array<string, string> $link";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}i:6;O:46:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Generic":2:{s:7:"␀*␀name";s:11:"psalm-param";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:27:"array<string, string> $link";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:7:"hasMany";O:27:"yii\apidoc\models\MethodDoc":26:{s:10:"isAbstract";b:0;s:7:"isFinal";b:0;s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:9:"definedBy";s:23:"yii\db\BaseActiveRecord";s:10:"sourceCode";s:103:"public function hasMany($class, $link)
