for MySQL, PostgreSQL and CUBRID databases. Defaults to null, meaning using default charset
as configured by the database.

For Oracle Database, the charset must be specified in the [[dsn]], for example for UTF-8 by appending `;charset=UTF-8`
to the DSN string.

The same applies for if you're using GBK or BIG5 charset with MySQL, then it's highly recommended to
specify charset via [[dsn]] like `'mysql:dbname=mydatabase;host=127.0.0.1;charset=GBK;'`.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\String_":0:{}i:1;O:36:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Null_":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:521:"the charset used for database connection. The property is only used
for MySQL, PostgreSQL and CUBRID databases. Defaults to null, meaning using default charset
as configured by the database.

For Oracle Database, the charset must be specified in the [[dsn]], for example for UTF-8 by appending `;charset=UTF-8`
to the DSN string.

The same applies for if you're using GBK or BIG5 charset with MySQL, then it's highly recommended to
specify charset via [[dsn]] like `'mysql:dbname=mydatabase;host=127.0.0.1;charset=GBK;'`.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:15:"$emulatePrepare";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:9:"bool|null";s:5:"types";a:2:{i:0;s:4:"bool";i:1;s:4:"null";}s:12:"defaultValue";N;s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:17:"yii\db\Connection";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:180271;s:4:"name";s:15:"$emulatePrepare";s:8:"fullName";s:34:"yii\db\Connection::$emulatePrepare";s:10:"sourceFile";s:92:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/Connection.php";s:9:"startLine";i:261;s:7:"endLine";i:261;s:16:"shortDescription";s:37:"Whether to turn on prepare emulation.";s:11:"description";s:367:"Whether to turn on prepare emulation. Defaults to false, meaning PDO
will use the native prepare support if available. For some databases (such as MySQL),
this may need to be set true so that PDO can emulate the prepare support to bypass
the buggy native prepare support.
The default value is null, which means the PDO ATTR_EMULATE_PREPARES value will not be changed.";s:5:"since";N;s:8:"sinceMap";a:0:{}s:15:"deprecatedSince";N;s:16:"deprecatedReason";N;s:4:"tags";a:1:{i:0;O:43:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Tags\Var_":4:{s:15:"␀*␀variableName";s:0:"";s:7:"␀*␀type";O:39:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Compound":2:{s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀types";a:2:{i:0;O:38:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Boolean":0:{}i:1;O:36:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\Null_":0:{}}s:52:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\Types\AggregatedType␀token";s:1:"|";}s:7:"␀*␀name";s:3:"var";s:14:"␀*␀description";O:45:"phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description":2:{s:59:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀bodyTemplate";s:367:"whether to turn on prepare emulation. Defaults to false, meaning PDO
will use the native prepare support if available. For some databases (such as MySQL),
this may need to be set true so that PDO can emulate the prepare support to bypass
the buggy native prepare support.
The default value is null, which means the PDO ATTR_EMULATE_PREPARES value will not be changed.";s:51:"␀phpDocumentor\Reflection\DocBlock\Description␀tags";a:0:{}}}}s:5:"todos";a:0:{}}s:12:"$tablePrefix";O:29:"yii\apidoc\models\PropertyDoc":22:{s:10:"visibility";s:6:"public";s:8:"isStatic";b:0;s:4:"type";s:6:"string";s:5:"types";a:1:{i:0;s:6:"string";}s:12:"defaultValue";s:2:"''";s:6:"getter";N;s:6:"setter";N;s:9:"definedBy";s:17:"yii\db\Connection";s:13:"phpDocContext";r:180271;s:4:"name";s:12:"$tablePrefix";s:8:"fullName";s:31:"yii\db\Connection::$tablePrefix";s:10:"sourceFile";s:92:"/home/mspirkov/open-source/yiisoft/yiiframework.com/data/yii-2.0/framework/db/Connection.php";s:9:"startLine";i:267;s:7:"endLine";i:267;s:16:"shortDescription";s:44:"The common prefix or suffix for table names.";s:11:"description";s:216:"The common prefix or suffix for table names. If a table name is given
